From: Solaris Codex maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Keep model-visible web.run compatible with its reserved schema

GPT-6.2 advertises experimental literature search, but the service rejects
that field in the reserved model-visible web.run declaration. This prevents
all turns, including shell-only requests, on the SPARC direct-tools path.
The same failure is reproducible on x64 when selecting direct tools.

Normalize only the model-request copy of web.run before code-mode schema
augmentation. Also normalize historical additional_tools declarations in the
request copy: a previously rejected declaration otherwise breaks resume even
with a corrected current schema. Never rewrite saved history, and avoid
cloning already-compatible catalogs. Preserve ordinary search, model metadata,
the registered executor, and the full nested Code Mode schema. Do not disable
web search or change transport, V8, or architecture selection.

Cover both capability values, other tool identities, classic/raw/Responses
Lite encodings, saved history preservation, and idempotent normalization.
Update the standalone search scenario and app-server schema expectations.

Related upstream report: https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/59782

